│                                                                                                                      │
│ Review background:                                                                                                   │
│ Ovarian cancer (OC) has the highest case fatality rate of all gynaecological cancers. Diagnostic delays are caused   │
│ by non‐specific symptoms. Existing systematic reviews have not comprehensively covered tests in current practice,    │
│ not estimated accuracy separately in pre‐ and postmenopausal women, or used inappropriate meta‐analytic methods.     │
│                                                                                                                      │
│ Review objective:                                                                                                    │
